  "quirks": [
    "The graph contains BOTH designated (is_designated=true) AND non-designated (is_designated=false) rows on all designation types. Non-designated rows represent tracts/areas HUD evaluated but did not select. Always filter with x.is_designated = true.",
    "basis_boost_pct is INTEGER with values 0 or 30. Never compare to '30%'. Use: x.basis_boost_pct = 30.",
    "CensusTract.county_fips is a 5-digit STRING (e.g. '48113'). CensusTract.fips_code is an 11-digit STRING (e.g. '48113017819'). Never confuse these.",
    "County has no cbsa_code property. To resolve a county by name convert it to county_fips. Examples: Dallas TX=48113, Travis TX=48453, LA CA=06037, Cook IL=17031.",
    "To filter tracts by county use CensusTract.county_fips directly: MATCH (ct:CensusTract {county_fips: $county_fips}). Do NOT traverse through a County node just to filter by county.",
    "MetroArea.cbsa_title is NULL for almost all nodes. For a human-readable metro name use SDDADesignation.area_name or NMDDADesignation.area_name instead.",
    "For point-in-time designation checks use designation_year = $year (equality). Do NOT use designation_year <= $year.",
    "Section8AMILimit and StateAMILimit are WIDE FORMAT -- all 8 household size limits (limit_1person through limit_8person) are columns on a single row. bedroom_count does not exist. max_rent is a direct column.",
    "LenderBehaviorRisk DEDUPLICATION -- some MetroArea nodes have multiple LenderBehaviorRisk records (one per Metropolitan Division). Deduplicate by ORDER BY r.total_applications DESC LIMIT 1 for single-year queries.",
    "HMDA trend queries: match LenderBehaviorRisk via MetroArea directly -- MATCH (m:MetroArea {cbsa_code: $cbsa_code})<-[:APPLIES_TO]-(r:LenderBehaviorRisk). Do not start from CensusTract.",
    "DDA means BOTH SDDADesignation (metro, via CensusTract-[:IN_METRO]->MetroArea) AND NMDDADesignation (non-metro, via CensusTract-[:IN_COUNTY]->County). Always check both. A metro tract will never match NMDDADesignation; a rural tract will never match SDDADesignation.",
    "program_type for Section8AMILimit and StateAMILimit: ELI (30% AMI), VLI (50% AMI), LI (80% AMI).",
    "denial_rate_disparity_ratio = denial_rate_minority / denial_rate_white. is_high_disparity = true when disparity_ratio > 2.0. risk_tier: low (<0.75), moderate (0.75-1.0), elevated (1.0-1.5), high (>1.5)."
  ]
